{
  "_README": "INERT reference copy of this repo's hook registrations \u2014\u2014 nothing loads this file; it is documentation. The live registrations are in ~/.claude/settings.json (USER level), NOT in this folder's settings.json (project level), because the Claude Desktop app executes user-level hooks but silently ignores project-level ones. Each script self-scopes to this repo via the payload cwd, so global registration is safe. It lives in .claude/ rather than cscpt/ because cscpt/ holds runnable scripts only. To restore on a new machine: merge the \"hooks\" object below into ~/.claude/settings.json and fix the absolute paths. Note the naming convention: the registered PostToolUse entries are the *_hook.sh bash fast-paths, each of which spawns its same-named .py lint only when the payload is relevant.",
